# Windows PowerShell terminal commands

The default shell in this environment is **Windows PowerShell**. In **Windows PowerShell 5.1** (common on Windows 10), `&&` is **not** a valid statement separator and causes:

`The token '&&' is not a valid statement separator in this version.`

## Do this instead

- **Chain commands** with a semicolon: `cd C:\projects\mui-tailwind\frontend; yarn lint`
- **Or** run `cd` and the command as **two separate** terminal invocations.

## Examples

```powershell
# ❌ BAD (fails on Windows PowerShell 5.1)
cd C:\projects\mui-tailwind\frontend && yarn lint

# ✅ GOOD
cd C:\projects\mui-tailwind\frontend; yarn lint
```

PowerShell 7+ supports `&&`; prefer `;` here so commands work regardless of version.
